<!--{ ri01 : rich }-->
# 3. Rich text

New lines are **rich text**: you write and format text as in Word, and bold
is bold while you type. This lesson has no checks: Stilo cannot see
formatting, so you try each step and look at the result. About four minutes.
<!--{ ri02 : markdown }-->
## The toolbar

Select a line and press **Enter**: a toolbar appears above it.

| Toolbar | What it does |
|---------|--------------|
| Style menu | Normal text, Heading 1 to 3, or Code |
| **B**, *I*, U, S | Bold, italic, underline, strikethrough |
| x<sub>2</sub>, x<sup>2</sup> | Subscript and superscript, as in f<sub>ck</sub> or m<sup>2</sup> |
| Lists and quote | A bulleted list, a numbered list, an indented quote |
| Link | A link on the selected text |
| ƒ, ∑ | A formula (lesson 4), an equation (lesson 6) |

Word's keys work too: **Ctrl+B**, **Ctrl+I**, **Ctrl+U** for bold, italic
and underline, **Ctrl+Alt+1** to **3** for headings (**Ctrl+Alt+0** for
normal text), **Ctrl+K** for a link, and **Tab** or **Shift+Tab** to indent
a list item.
<!--{ ri03 : rich }-->
## Try it

Select the empty line just below this one, press **Enter**, and:

1. Type `# ` (a hash and a space) and then *My notes*: the line becomes a
   heading. Press **Enter** for a new paragraph.
2. Type `- ` (a dash and a space) and two items, pressing **Enter** after
   the first: a bulleted list.
3. Select a word and press **Ctrl+B** to make it bold.
4. Select another word, press **Ctrl+K**, type `https://www.onlabs.org`
   and press **Enter**: a link.
5. Press **Ctrl+Enter** to keep it all.
<!--{ ri04 : rich }-->

<!--{ ri05 : rich }-->
## Markdown underneath

A rich text line is saved as **Markdown**, a simple way to write formatting
with ordinary characters: `**bold**`, `# Heading`, `- item`. Select the line
you just wrote and press **m**: you see and edit its Markdown. Press **r** to
go back to rich text; the text does not change. Lesson 5 tells more about the
types of lines.

Rich text has no colours, fonts or alignment, as a report written to a
standard needs none. Images show but cannot be inserted in rich text: write
them in Markdown (lesson 8).

More in the manual: [Writing text](https://www.onlabs.org/manual/editor/writing.html).
<!--{ ri06 : rich }-->
